Persistent biometric unlock for the Bitwarden Desktop Linux client, as a patch
against the *compiled* OsBiometricsServiceLinux block inside app.asar's main.js.

Upstream (2026.8.0) already ships the scaffolding — the "Bitwarden_biometric"
service name is referenced elsewhere, and enrollPersistent/hasPersistentKey exist
as stubs returning nothing and false. This fills them in: the unlock key is stored
in the FreeDesktop Secret Service, so a YubiKey/FIDO2 session survives a restart.
The TypeScript counterpart is 01-linux-persistent-biometrics.patch.

Applied by scripts/patch-biometrics-compiled.py, which slices the block out of
main.js, patches it and splices it back. The slice anchors (`class
OsBiometricsServiceLinux`, `exports["default"] = ...`) are not minified by tsc,
so they survive upstream releases; the hunks themselves may need a refresh when
upstream edits this class.

Generated against Bitwarden 2026.8.0 (Bitwarden-2026.8.0-amd64.deb,
sha256 720ecc392eef1992780af2aaabd4733916807155c8ee217ed67f3f93287bb415).

